---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Stock screen
// (project/AdminStock.dc.html -> NavSidebar role="admin" active="Stock"
// + the plain shared NavTop.astro (section="Inventory" page="Stock") +
// PageStock, a role-agnostic, admin-only component — same situation as
// Product Info's PageProductDetail: no role prop, AdminStock.dc.html is
// its only real consumer).
//
// SCHEMA REALITY vs THE DESIGN: PageStock.dc.html assumes the same
// warehouse-management model already found not to exist when building
// Admin Product Info — per-bin locations, reserved/available-to-promise
// quantities, and a restock-REQUEST-and-fulfilment system (the header's
// "restock requests go to inventory staff" claim and each row's "Request
// restock (sent to inventory staff)" button). None of that exists: real
// restocking is `record_inventory_movement()`, a direct action, not a
// request-routing workflow. Every one of those is omitted or replaced
// with an honest "—", never invented.
//
// Real vs deferred/fabricated, per your explicit no-fabrication rules:
//  - Header: "Export" omitted (no real export capability, same precedent
//    as every other Admin list screen). Subtitle drops the fabricated
//    "main warehouse"/"restock requests go to inventory staff"/"updated 2
//    min ago" claims, replaced with a plain honest description.
//  - "Stock adjustment" button: genuinely real and already authorized —
//    inventory_update_staff / inventory_movements_insert_staff RLS
//    includes admin (and super_admin), identical to inventory_staff (see
//    migrations/0005). Reuses the EXACT same real
//    `recordInventoryMovement` Action → `record_inventory_movement()` RPC
//    already proven on /inventory/adjustments — same product search,
//    reason chips (Damaged forces a negative delta, matching the RPC's
//    own -abs() behavior), quantity stepper, live "current → new qty"
//    preview, same client+server validation, same real audit trail (every
//    movement is attributed to the real signed-in admin via
//    `performed_by`). Packaged as a toggle panel (hidden until opened)
//    rather than an always-visible side column, since this screen's
//    primary content is the stock table itself, not a dedicated
//    adjustment workflow the way /inventory/adjustments is.
//  - Stat strip (5 real stats, all admin-appropriate real KPIs):
//    "Inventory value" — the exact same real `inventory_value_summary`
//    view (sum of qty×price for active products) already used on Admin
//    Dashboard, honestly labelled "at price" (NOT "at cost" — the
//    design's own label doesn't match what this view actually computes,
//    and products.cost is null for some real rows anyway, so relabelling
//    honestly was preferred over inventing a second cost-based figure).
//    "SKUs" — real total product count + real populated-category count.
//    "Low stock"/"Out of stock" — real counts (identical qty<=reorder_level
//    computation used everywhere else); their fabricated notes ("restock
//    requested for 5", "2 restocks due this week") dropped — no
//    restock-request system exists. "Dead stock (90 days)" — genuinely
//    real and derivable: active products with zero inventory_movements
//    in the real last-90-IST-days window (resolveDashboardRange("90d"),
//    the exact same shared IST-safe helper every other dashboard in this
//    project already uses — no UTC/IST shifting reintroduced), real ₹
//    value (at price) + real SKU count of that set.
//  - "Stock value by category": real, grouped from the same real active
//    products, same "at price" honest relabel as above, real bar widths
//    scaled to the largest real category value (not fabricated
//    percentages).
//  - Status tabs (All/Low stock/Out of stock): real counts, real filter.
//  - "Category"/"Supplier" facets: real — Category from real
//    categories.name; Supplier reuses the exact same "most recent
//    restock supplier" derivation already proven on Admin Products/
//    Product Info (the only place a supplier is ever attached to a
//    product in this schema).
//  - Table: SKU/Product (real, product name links to the real, already-
//    approved /admin/products/[id] — not /sales/products or
//    /inventory/products), On hand/Low at/Status all real. "Bin" column:
//    no location field exists — kept in the grid (matches the design's
//    own shape) but every cell honestly shows "—", same precedent already
//    established on Stock Adjustments' own Location/Bin cells. "Reserved"/
//    "Available": no reservation or available-to-promise concept exists
//    — both kept as honest "—" columns rather than computed from a
//    fabricated "reserved" (which would make "Available" a fabricated
//    derived number too, exactly what your instructions explicitly
//    forbid). "Level" bar: real substitute — on-hand relative to
//    2×reorder_level (design used the fabricated "available" for this;
//    on-hand is the real genuine equivalent). "Actions": only "Adjust"
//    kept (opens the real panel above, pre-selecting that row's product);
//    "Request restock" omitted entirely — no request workflow and no
//    honest destination exists (same reasoning as Product Info's own
//    "Request restock" omission).
//  - Footer: "Showing 8 of 3,418 SKUs · sorted by availability" and the
//    fake "Page 1 of 428" pagination replaced with a real "{N} of {M}
//    products" count (same precedent as every other Admin list screen —
//    no fake pagination). Real default sort: stock-status severity (out
//    → low → in) then name — an honest, genuinely useful real substitute
//    for the fabricated "sorted by availability" (availability itself
//    doesn't exist as a real field).
//  - "View" grid/list toggle: omitted — no view-mode capability, same
//    precedent as every other list screen in this project.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";
import { resolveDashboardRange } from "../../../lib/dashboardRange";

const url = Astro.url;
const search = url.searchParams.get("search")?.trim() ?? "";
const category = url.searchParams.get("category") ?? "";
const status = url.searchParams.get("status") ?? "";
const supplier = url.searchParams.get("supplier") ?? "";
const viewerRole = (Astro.locals.role === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

// --- Real full catalog (active AND inactive — same precedent as Admin Products) ---
const { data: productRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("products")
  .select("id, sku, name, price, is_active, category_id, categories(name), inventory(quantity_on_hand, reorder_level)")
  .order("name");

const { data: restockRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("inventory_movements")
  .select("product_id, created_at, suppliers(name)")
  .eq("movement_type", "restock")
  .not("supplier_id", "is", null)
  .order("created_at", { ascending: false });

const supplierByProduct = new Map<string, string>();
for (const r of restockRows ?? []) {
  if (supplierByProduct.has(r.product_id as string)) continue;
  const name = (r.suppliers as unknown as { name: string } | null)?.name;
  if (name) supplierByProduct.set(r.product_id as string, name);
}

// --- Real "last movement" per product, for the real Dead stock (90d) stat ---
const { data: lastMoveRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("inventory_movements")
  .select("product_id, created_at")
  .order("created_at", { ascending: false });
const lastMovementByProduct = new Map<string, string>();
for (const r of lastMoveRows ?? []) {
  if (!lastMovementByProduct.has(r.product_id as string)) lastMovementByProduct.set(r.product_id as string, r.created_at as string);
}

function categoryOf(row: { categories: unknown }): { name: string } | null {
  return row.categories as unknown as { name: string } | null;
}
function inventoryOf(row: { inventory: unknown }): { quantity_on_hand: number; reorder_level: number } | null {
  const inv = row.inventory as unknown as { quantity_on_hand: number; reorder_level: number }[] | null;
  return inv?.[0] ?? null;
}

const formatCurrency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN", { style: "currency", currency: "INR", maximumFractionDigits: 2 }).format(value);
const formatCompact = (value: number) => {
  if (value >= 10000000) return `₹${(value / 10000000).toFixed(1)}Cr`;
  if (value >= 100000) return `₹${(value / 100000).toFixed(1)}L`;
  return formatCurrency(value);
};

const allProducts = (productRows ?? []).map((p) => {
  const inv = inventoryOf(p);
  const qty = inv?.quantity_on_hand ?? 0;
  const reorderLevel = inv?.reorder_level ?? 0;
  const stockTone: "in" | "low" | "out" = qty === 0 ? "out" : qty <= reorderLevel ? "low" : "in";
  const stockSeverity = stockTone === "out" ? 0 : stockTone === "low" ? 1 : 2;
  return {
    id: p.id,
    sku: p.sku,
    name: p.name,
    isActive: p.is_active,
    categoryId: p.category_id as string | null,
    categoryName: categoryOf(p)?.name ?? "Uncategorised",
    price: Number(p.price),
    qty,
    reorderLevel,
    stockTone,
    stockSeverity,
    supplier: supplierByProduct.get(p.id) ?? null,
    lastMovementAt: lastMovementByProduct.get(p.id) ?? null,
  };
});

const STOCK_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { in: "In stock", low: "Low stock", out: "Out of stock" };

// --- Real stat strip ---
const inventoryValueAtPrice = allProducts.filter((p) => p.isActive).reduce((sum, p) => sum + p.qty * p.price, 0);
const totalSkus = allProducts.length;
const populatedCategoryCount = new Set(allProducts.filter((p) => p.categoryId).map((p) => p.categoryId)).size;
const lowStockCount = allProducts.filter((p) => p.stockTone === "low").length;
const outOfStockCount = allProducts.filter((p) => p.stockTone === "out").length;

const ninetyDayRange = resolveDashboardRange("90d");
const deadStockProducts = allProducts.filter(
  (p) => p.isActive && (!p.lastMovementAt || new Date(p.lastMovementAt) < new Date(ninetyDayRange.from!))
);
const deadStockValue = deadStockProducts.reduce((sum, p) => sum + p.qty * p.price, 0);

const stats = [
  { label: "Inventory value", value: formatCompact(inventoryValueAtPrice), note: "at price", tone: "" },
  { label: "SKUs", value: String(totalSkus), note: `in ${populatedCategoryCount} categor${populatedCategoryCount === 1 ? "y" : "ies"}`, tone: "" },
  { label: "Low stock", value: String(lowStockCount), note: "store-wide", tone: "warn" },
  { label: "Out of stock", value: String(outOfStockCount), note: "store-wide", tone: "danger" },
  { label: "Dead stock (90 days)", value: formatCompact(deadStockValue), note: `${deadStockProducts.length} SKU${deadStockProducts.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}, no movement`, tone: "" },
];

// --- Real stock value by category ---
const categoryValues = new Map<string, number>();
for (const p of allProducts.filter((p) => p.isActive)) {
  categoryValues.set(p.categoryName, (categoryValues.get(p.categoryName) ?? 0) + p.qty * p.price);
}
const categoryValueList = [...categoryValues.entries()].sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1]);
const maxCategoryValue = Math.max(...categoryValueList.map(([, v]) => v), 1);
const categoryBars = categoryValueList.map(([name, value]) => ({
  name,
  value: formatCompact(value),
  pct: Math.round((value / maxCategoryValue) * 100),
}));

// --- Real category/supplier facet options ---
const categoryOptions = [...new Map(allProducts.filter((p) => p.categoryId).map((p) => [p.categoryId!, p.categoryName])).entries()]
  .map(([id, name]) => ({ id, name }))
  .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const supplierOptions = [...new Set(allProducts.map((p) => p.supplier).filter((s): s is string => !!s))].sort((a, b) => a.localeCompare(b));

// --- Real status tabs (matches the design's own 3-tab set: All/Low/Out) ---
const STATUS_TABS = [
  { key: "", label: "All", count: allProducts.length },
  { key: "low", label: "Low stock", count: lowStockCount },
  { key: "out", label: "Out of stock", count: outOfStockCount },
];

// --- Real filter + sort ---
let filtered = allProducts.filter((p) => {
  if (category && p.categoryId !== category) return false;
  if (status && p.stockTone !== status) return false;
  if (supplier && p.supplier !== supplier) return false;
  if (!search) return true;
  const needle = search.toLowerCase();
  return p.name.toLowerCase().includes(needle) || p.sku.toLowerCase().includes(needle);
});
filtered = [...filtered].sort((a, b) => a.stockSeverity - b.stockSeverity || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));

function buildUrl(overrides: Record<string, string | undefined>) {
  const next = new URLSearchParams(url.search);
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(overrides)) {
    if (value) next.set(key, value);
    else next.delete(key);
  }
  const qs = next.toString();
  return qs ? `/admin/stock?${qs}` : "/admin/stock";
}

// --- Real "Level" bar (genuine on-hand-relative substitute for the
// design's fabricated available-to-promise bar) ---
function levelPct(qty: number, reorderLevel: number): number {
  if (reorderLevel <= 0) return qty > 0 ? 100 : 0;
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round((qty / (reorderLevel * 2)) * 100)));
}
const LEVEL_COLOR: Record<string, string> = { in: "var(--sd-success-fg)", low: "var(--sd-warn-fg)", out: "var(--sd-danger-fg)" };

// --- Data passed to the client for the real product search inside the
// Stock adjustment panel (same shape/technique already used by
// /inventory/adjustments and /admin/orders/new) ---
const adjustmentProducts = allProducts.map((p) => ({ id: p.id, sku: p.sku, name: p.name, qty: p.qty, stockTone: p.stockTone }));
---

<BaseLayout title="Stock — Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Stock" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Inventory" page="Stock" searchAction="/admin/stock" searchName="search" searchValue={search} searchPlaceholder="Filter by SKU or product…" />

      <main id="main-content" class="st__main">
        <div class="st__header">
          <div class="st__heading-col">
            <h1>Stock</h1>
            <span class="st__subtitle">Store-wide stock levels</span>
          </div>
          <button type="button" id="st-open-adjust" class="st__adjust-btn">
            <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h10M18 6h2M4 12h4M12 12h8M4 18h12M14 4v4M8 10v4M16 16v4"></path></svg>
            Stock adjustment
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="st__stats">
          {stats.map((s) => (
            <div class="st__stat-card">
              <span class="st__stat-label">{s.label}</span>
              <span class={`st__stat-value ${s.tone ? `st__stat-value--${s.tone}` : ""}`}>{s.value}</span>
              <span class="st__stat-note">{s.note}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="st__cat-card">
          <div class="st__cat-head">
            <span class="st__cat-title">Stock value by category</span>
            <span class="st__cat-sub">At price · total {formatCompact(inventoryValueAtPrice)}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="st__cat-bars" role="img" aria-label={`Stock value by category: ${categoryBars.map((c) => `${c.name} ${c.value}`).join(", ")}`}>
            {categoryBars.map((c) => (
              <div class="st__cat-row">
                <span class="st__cat-label">{c.name}</span>
                <div class="st__cat-track"><div class="st__cat-fill" style={`width: ${c.pct}%;`} /></div>
                <span class="st__cat-value">{c.value}</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="st__toolbar">
          <div role="tablist" aria-label="Stock status" class="st__tabs">
            {STATUS_TABS.map((t) => (
              <a href={buildUrl({ status: t.key || undefined })} role="tab" aria-selected={status === t.key} class={status === t.key ? "is-active" : ""}>
                {t.label} <span class="st__tab-count">{t.count}</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
          <select id="st-category-filter" class="st__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by category">
            <option value={buildUrl({ category: undefined })} selected={!category}>+ Category</option>
            {categoryOptions.map((c) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ category: c.id })} selected={category === c.id}>{c.name}</option>
            ))}
          </select>
          <select id="st-supplier-filter" class="st__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by supplier">
            <option value={buildUrl({ supplier: undefined })} selected={!supplier}>+ Supplier</option>
            {supplierOptions.map((s) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ supplier: s })} selected={supplier === s}>{s}</option>
            ))}
          </select>
        </div>

        {
          filtered.length > 0 ? (
            <div class="st__panel">
              <div class="st__grid st__grid-head">
                <span>SKU</span><span>Product</span><span>Bin</span><span class="st__col-right">On hand</span><span class="st__col-right">Reserved</span><span class="st__col-right">Available</span><span class="st__col-right">Low at</span><span>Level</span><span>Status</span><span class="st__col-right">Actions</span>
              </div>
              {filtered.map((p) => (
                <div class="st__grid st__row">
                  <span class="st__muted-cell">{p.sku}</span>
                  <a href={`/admin/products/${p.id}`} class="st__name-cell">
                    {p.name}
                    {!p.isActive && <span class="st__inactive-tag">Inactive</span>}
                  </a>
                  <span class="st__muted-cell">—</span>
                  <span class="st__col-right st__on-hand">{p.qty}</span>
                  <span class="st__col-right st__muted-cell">—</span>
                  <span class="st__col-right st__muted-cell">—</span>
                  <span class="st__col-right st__muted-cell">{p.reorderLevel}</span>
                  <span class="st__level-track" role="img" aria-label={`${levelPct(p.qty, p.reorderLevel)}% of target level`}>
                    <span class="st__level-fill" style={`width: ${levelPct(p.qty, p.reorderLevel)}%; background: ${LEVEL_COLOR[p.stockTone]};`} />
                  </span>
                  <span><span class={`st__pill st__pill--${p.stockTone}`}>{STOCK_LABEL[p.stockTone]}</span></span>
                  <span class="st__row-actions">
                    <button type="button" class="st__adjust-icon-btn" aria-label={`Adjust ${p.name}`} title="Adjust" data-product-id={p.id}>
                      <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h10M18 6h2M4 12h4M12 12h8M4 18h12M14 4v4M8 10v4M16 16v4"></path></svg>
                    </button>
                  </span>
                </div>
              ))}
              <div class="st__panel-footer">{filtered.length} of {allProducts.length} product{allProducts.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} · sorted by stock status</div>
            </div>
          ) : (
            <div class="st__empty">
              <p class="st__empty-title">No stock rows found</p>
              <p class="st__empty-body">Try a different search or filter.</p>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </main>
    </div>

    <div id="st-adjust-backdrop" class="st__adjust-backdrop" hidden></div>
    <aside id="st-adjust-panel" class="st__adjust-panel" hidden aria-label="Stock adjustment">
      <div class="st__adjust-panel-head">
        <h2>Stock adjustment</h2>
        <button type="button" id="st-close-adjust" aria-label="Close" class="st__adjust-close">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
      <span class="st__adjust-panel-sub">Search the item, then record what changed.</span>

      <div class="st__field-col">
        <label for="st-adj-search">Product</label>
        <div class="st__product-search-wrap">
          <input type="search" id="st-adj-search" class="st__product-search" placeholder="Search by name or SKU…" aria-label="Search products" autocomplete="off" />
          <div id="st-adj-results" class="st__picker-results" role="listbox" aria-label="Products" hidden></div>
        </div>
        <div id="st-adj-selected" class="st__selected-product" hidden>
          <span id="st-adj-selected-name" class="st__selected-name"></span>
          <button type="button" id="st-adj-clear" aria-label="Clear product" class="st__clear-btn">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="st__field-col">
        <span>Current qty</span>
        <div class="st__static-cell" id="st-adj-current-qty">—</div>
      </div>

      <div class="st__field-col">
        <span id="st-adj-reason-label">Reason</span>
        <div role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="st-adj-reason-label" class="st__reasons" id="st-adj-reasons">
          {["Damaged", "Lost", "Found", "Expired", "Count correction"].map((label) => (
            <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="st__reason-chip" data-reason={label}>{label}</button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <span class="st__hint">Damaged saves this as a damage record.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="st__field-col">
        <span>Quantity change</span>
        <div class="st__qty-row">
          <div class="st__stepper">
            <button type="button" id="st-adj-dec" aria-label="Decrease by 1" class="st__stepper-btn">−</button>
            <input type="text" inputmode="numeric" id="st-adj-qty" aria-label="Quantity change" class="st__qty-input" />
            <button type="button" id="st-adj-inc" aria-label="Increase by 1" class="st__stepper-btn">+</button>
          </div>
          <div class="st__preview">
            <span class="st__preview-label">New qty</span>
            <span id="st-adj-preview" class="st__preview-value">Select a product</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="st__field-col">
        <label for="st-adj-note">Note</label>
        <textarea id="st-adj-note" class="st__textarea" placeholder="What did you check or do?"></textarea>
      </div>

      <p id="st-adj-message" class="st__status-message" role="status" />

      <div class="st__adjust-actions">
        <button type="button" id="st-adj-cancel" class="st__btn">Cancel</button>
        <button type="button" id="st-adj-submit" class="st__btn st__btn--primary" disabled>Submit adjustment</button>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <div id="st-adjust-data" hidden data-products={JSON.stringify(adjustmentProducts)}></div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sd {
    --sd-shell: #fafafa;
    --sd-panel: #ffffff;
    --sd-card: #ffffff;
    --sd-fg: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-fg2: #404040;
    --sd-muted: #f5f5f5;
    --sd-muted-fg: #737373;
    --sd-border: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-input: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-primary: #171717;
    --sd-primary-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-success-bg: #ecfdf3;
    --sd-success-fg: #15803d;
    --sd-warn-bg: #fef3e2;
    --sd-warn-fg: #9a3412;
    --sd-danger-bg: #feecec;
    --sd-danger-fg: #b91c1c;
    --sd-info-bg: #eef2ff;
    --sd-info-fg: #3538cd;
    --sd-accent: #2b50e0;
    --sd-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    color-scheme: light;

    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font-family: "Geist", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sd[data-theme="dark"] {
    --sd-shell: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-panel: #0f0f0f;
    --sd-card: #171717;
    --sd-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-fg2: #d4d4d4;
    --sd-muted: #262626;
